Fix GameLoopLab.svelte — it's broken and unusable. Multiple critical issues:

## 1. ALL CSS variables are wrong — nothing renders correctly

The component uses CSS variables that DO NOT EXIST in the parent Workbench.svelte. Replace every single one:

WRONG → CORRECT:
- `var(--bg-app)` → `var(--bg)`
- `var(--bg-card)` → `var(--bg-card)` (this one is correct)
- `var(--bg-elevated)` → `var(--bg-muted)`
- `var(--bg-hover)` → `var(--bg-accent)`
- `var(--text-primary)` → `var(--fg)`
- `var(--text-muted)` → `var(--fg-muted)`
- `var(--text-gold)` → `var(--accent-amber)`
- `var(--text-red)` → `var(--accent-red)`
- `var(--text-green)` → `var(--accent-green)`
- `var(--text-cyan)` → `var(--accent)`
- `var(--accent-cyan)` → `var(--accent)` (parent uses --accent for cyan)
- `var(--accent-purple)` → `var(--accent)` (no purple token exists)
- `var(--accent-yellow)` → `var(--accent-amber)`
- `var(--accent-orange)` → `var(--accent-amber)`
- `var(--text-sm)` → remove, use literal `11px`
- `var(--text-xs)` → remove, use literal `10px`
- `var(--text-base)` → remove, use literal `12px`
- `var(--text-lg)` → remove, use literal `14px`
- `var(--text-xl)` → remove, use literal `16px`
- `var(--text-2xl)` → remove, use literal `20px`

The available tokens from Workbench.svelte are ONLY:
--bg, --bg-card, --bg-muted, --bg-accent, --border, --border-muted, --border-accent, --fg, --fg-muted, --fg-dim, --accent, --accent-green, --accent-amber, --accent-red, --radius-sm, --radius, --radius-lg, --space-xs, --space-sm, --space-md, --space-lg, --space-xl, --font-mono, --transition-fast, --transition

## 2. Auto run must LOOP — town → dungeon → town → dungeon → repeat

Current auto run does one dungeon run then stops. Change it to be a continuous loop:
- Start in town
- Auto-start a run
- Simulate all floors
- End run → run_complete
- Process loot → return to town
- Advance day
- Wait 1 second in town
- Start next run automatically
- Keep looping until user clicks "Stop Auto"

The `autoRun` function should use `setTimeout` chains (not setInterval) for clearer control:

```js
let autoRunning = false;

async function autoRun() {
  autoRunning = true;
  addLogEntry('Auto-run started — looping town ↔ dungeon', 'phase');
  autoStep();
}

function autoStep() {
  if (!autoRunning) return;

  if (phase === 'town') {
    startRun();
    setTimeout(autoStep, 400);
  } else if (phase === 'dungeon') {
    simulateFloor();
    setTimeout(autoStep, 400);
  } else if (phase === 'floor_complete') {
    if (run.floor < run.maxFloors) {
      nextFloor();
    } else {
      endCurrentRun('cleared');
    }
    setTimeout(autoStep, 400);
  } else if (phase === 'run_complete') {
    returnToTown();
    setTimeout(autoStep, 1000); // pause in town
  }
}

function stopAutoRun() {
  autoRunning = false;
  addLogEntry('Auto-run stopped', 'info');
}
```

Remove the old `autoRunInterval` / `setInterval` approach entirely.

## 3. Make the town phase actually useful and visible

The town phase should feel like arriving somewhere. Add:
- A welcome message showing the day
- Player gold prominently displayed
- Equipment section showing what's equipped with equip/unequip from stash
- The vendor should be populated (call refreshVendor when returning to town)
- Show the stash with item colors and levels

## 4. Phase indicator should show the LOOP clearly

Change the phase list from a linear list to show the circular nature:
```
Town → Dungeon → Floor Complete → Run Complete → Town (loops)
```
The active phase dot should pulse/glow.

## 5. Better visual hierarchy

- The floor title in dungeon phase should be prominent
- Floor complete should show a satisfying results card
- Run complete grade should be large and colorful
- Town cards should have clear headers and borders
- Log entries should be color-coded properly using the CORRECT tokens

## 6. Remove duplicate log function

There are two functions: `log()` and `addLogEntry()` that do the same thing. Remove `log()` and keep only `addLogEntry()`.

Do NOT change any imports or the lib modules. Only fix GameLoopLab.svelte.
